import{_ as t,c as a,o as n,ag as r}from"./chunks/framework.Vyheyqg9.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"JavaScript learning-notes assistant: independent milestones","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"practice/applied-ai/javascript-assistant.md","filePath":"practice/applied-ai/javascript-assistant.md"}'),i={name:"practice/applied-ai/javascript-assistant.md"};function s(o,e,d,l,c,p){return n(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="javascript-learning-notes-assistant-independent-milestones" tabindex="-1">JavaScript learning-notes assistant: independent milestones <a class="header-anchor" href="#javascript-learning-notes-assistant-independent-milestones" aria-label="Permalink to “JavaScript learning-notes assistant: independent milestones”">​</a></h1><p>This is the beginner project for <a href="./../../applied-ai/">Build AI Apps</a>. <strong>Every learner milestone remains outstanding.</strong> The <a href="./../../workbench/applied-ai/javascript/">workbench</a> is a worked reference; running it is not the same as implementing your own project.</p><p>Use a separate owned learner directory, synthetic notes and a small evidence ledger. Preserve any Autocode task&#39;s original scripts, exports, dependency configuration and supplied database settings. Never edit or add to <code>src/tests</code>. For a real submission run <code>npm run build</code>, <code>npm run test</code> and, for Module 4, its required Cobertura coverage script; this hub&#39;s JS IDs are not Autocode module numbers.</p><h2 id="build-in-small-increments" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">1 </span>Build in small increments <a class="header-anchor" href="#build-in-small-increments" aria-label="Permalink to “1 Build in small increments”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Deliverable</th><th>Checks and evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>JS-00</td><td>Explain request flow and set up a JS project</td><td>Draw browser/server/provider boundaries; keep a key out of frontend code; record actual runtime</td></tr><tr><td>JS-01</td><td>Console helper with injected fake, then optional provider</td><td>Valid/empty input, rejected request, clean exit; label mock versus live observations</td></tr><tr><td>JS-02</td><td>Chatbot inside an app</td><td>Completed-turn history, reset, failure, duplicate submit, delayed cancellation; demonstrate actual browser behavior</td></tr><tr><td>JS-03</td><td>Streaming extension after JS-02</td><td>Split network events, terminal success, partial failure, Stop, stale response after reset/unmount; do not call animated mock text provider streaming</td></tr><tr><td>JS-04</td><td>Structured note classifier</td><td>Exact allowed fields, invalid shape, fabricated/genuine-but-misleading quote, ambiguous review; separate semantic rubric</td></tr><tr><td>JS-05</td><td>Fixed read workflow, then a bounded model-selected tool loop</td><td>Allowed/unknown tool, invalid/extra args, call IDs/results, denied access, exhausted call/time limits; no unintended I/O</td></tr><tr><td>JS-06</td><td>Cited RAG integrated with the chatbot</td><td>Load/version/chunk notes; lexical baseline; no-evidence answer; source/citation checks; labeled exact/paraphrase/unsupported cases</td></tr><tr><td>JS-06B</td><td>Optional embedding/hosted-store comparison</td><td>Compatible model/dimensions/metric, ranks on the same frozen question set, update/delete and access cases; real adapter observations separate from hand vectors</td></tr><tr><td>JS-07</td><td>Your own MCP server and host connection</td><td>SDK discovery, allowed/bad tool calls, resource/prompt, child cleanup; record actual host setup separately from SDK-only checks</td></tr><tr><td>JS-08</td><td>Stateful graph and interruption</td><td>Conditional route, approve/reject, RAM restart loss; optionally reopen a durable checkpointer and test current ownership</td></tr><tr><td>JS-09</td><td>One chosen extension</td><td>Python processing, n8n, A2A or multimedia; scope, actual result, failure and remaining limits</td></tr></tbody></table><p>JS-03 may be deferred until a non-streaming RAG baseline works. JS-06B and JS-09 are optional. No paid model or hosted vector store is necessary to begin. By JS-06, actual generated answer quality needs a real authorized model experiment or an explicitly unmeasured outcome; a fake does not establish it.</p><h2 id="keep-one-evidence-record-per-increment" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">2 </span>Keep one evidence record per increment <a class="header-anchor" href="#keep-one-evidence-record-per-increment" aria-label="Permalink to “2 Keep one evidence record per increment”">​</a></h2><p>Record the requirement, code/lock/config version, expected outcome, actual command or interaction, observed result and unresolved gaps. Keep one meaningful failure/correction. For model work include prompt/model/corpus versions, allowed data and usage/unknown-cost notes. Never store credentials in the ledger.</p><p>At JS-02, explain local versus persisted history. At JS-05, distinguish a proposed call from actual execution. At JS-06, distinguish retrieval relevance, citation membership and claim support. At JS-08, distinguish a synthetic review value from trusted write approval. These are completion checks, not vocabulary-only questions.</p><h2 id="continue-into-deeper-engineering-when-useful" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">3 </span>Continue into deeper engineering when useful <a class="header-anchor" href="#continue-into-deeper-engineering-when-useful" aria-label="Permalink to “3 Continue into deeper engineering when useful”">​</a></h2><p>JS-06 can grow into <a href="./rag-assistant.html">P-334/RAG-1–4</a>; JS-05/08 can grow into <a href="./resumable-workflow.html">P-335/WF-1–4</a>. Those projects require stronger access, lifecycle and recovery evidence than this beginner route. The <a href="./../../python-for-ai/">Python companion</a> is optional; implement its version only for a concrete need. Existing IDs and historical observations remain intact.</p>',11)])])}const h=t(i,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,h as default};
